ansport rotation.\n\nDeclared roles: `orchestration`, `accessor`, `mapper`, `filter`, `validator`, `predicate`, `formatter`, `parser`.\n\n## Source scope\n\nThe functional S11 cutoff is `95699d6..1593ef8`. The audited net source range is `95699d6..7ec42d4`; it includes the post-cutoff revert/remediation commits, the transport-rotation fix, the launch heartbeat-gap supervision fix, and the committed S11 function-classification remediation. `2b7ab03` briefly added an out-of-scope private SQLite fallback for `scripts/opencode-turns`; `c3ab19c` reverts that content, and `1e043d3` restores the public-CLI script executable bit required by the workspace tests. `a1a3ca1` rotates external-provider transport/account-unavailable failures across the pool while keeping deterministic schema/protocol/policy failures terminal. `dc2900d` adds launch heartbeat-gap supervision and coverage. `7ec42d4` only splits helper responsibilities in already-touched files and records the gate artifacts; it does not add provider behavior or a state schema migration.\n\n`crates/oulipoly-provider/src/generated.rs` receives no generated-artifact exemption. It is treated as hand-maintained provider protocol DTO code for this gate, consistent with the S10B disposition.\n\nTouched files in scope are exactly `planning/s11-gate/gates/touched-files.txt`.\n\n## Touched-file roles\n\n| File | Declared roles | Role notes |\n|---|---|---|","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s11-gate/contracts/s11.contract.md","text":"# S11 Gate Contract\n\n## Component declared roles\n\nComponent: external provider wake delivery confirmation, detached resume continuity, and external transport rotation.\n\nDeclared roles: `orchestration`, `accessor`, `mapper`, `filter`, `validator`, `predicate`, `formatter`, `parser`.\n\n## Source scope\n\nThe functional S11 cutoff is `95699d6..1593ef8`. The audited net source range is `95699d6..7ec42d4`; it includes the post-cutoff revert/remediation commits, the transport-rotation fix, the launch heartbeat-gap supervision fix, and the committed S11 function-classification remediation. `2b7ab03` briefly added an out-of-scope private SQLite fallback for `scripts/opencode-turns`; `c3ab19c` reverts that content, and `1e043d3` restores the public-CLI script executable bit required by the workspace tests. `a1a3ca1` rotates external-provider transport/account-unavailable failures across the pool while keeping deterministic schema/protocol/policy failures terminal. `dc2900d` adds launch heartbeat-gap supervision and coverage. `7ec42d4` only splits helper responsibilities in already-touched files and records the gate artifacts; it does not add provider behavior or a state schema migration.\n\n`crates/oulipoly-provider/src/generated.rs` receives no generated-artifact exemption. It is treated as hand-maintained provider protocol DTO code for this gate, consistent with the S10B disposition.\n\nTouched files in scope are exactly `planning/s11-gate/gates/touched-files.txt`.\n\n## Touched-file roles\n\n| File | Declared roles | Role notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `DECISIONS.md` | `formatter` | Decision log context for validation/audit ratification; prose only. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/client.rs` | `accessor`, `mapper`, `orchestration` | Provider client invoke flow, process observer plumbing, and timeout/default mapping. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/error.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider error envelope parsing, typed diagnostics/status access, and error mapping. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/generated.rs` | `formatter`, `mapper`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider protocol DTOs and fixed discriminator/boolean validation. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/process.rs` | `accessor`, `mapper`, `orchestration` | Provider subprocess lifecycle and spawn-observer process identity capture. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/testkit.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider-crate testkit for fake-provider compilation, process-leak probing, mode mapping, and lifecycle assertions. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/tests/fixtures/provider_client/fake_provider.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Fake provider executable fixture for provider client protocol, launch stream, lifecycle, and heartbeat-gap tests. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-provider/tests/launch_stream_lifecycle.rs` | `accessor`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider launch lifecycle tests for cancellation, timeout cleanup, and heartbeat-gap behavior. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/cli.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration` | CLI executor environment/session orchestration and parent linkage handling. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/cli/result.rs` | `mapper`, `predicate` | Execution result/session capture DTO mapping and presence predicates. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/cli/spawn_identity.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `validator` | Process identity observation and sidecar owner/session persistence. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/context.rs` | `mapper`, `accessor` | External dispatch context and selected provider settings identity mapping. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/dispatch.rs` | `orchestration`, `mapper`, `accessor` | External provider policy/launch dispatch, process identity backfill, and result mapping. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/error_formatter.rs` | `formatter`, `accessor` | Stable external provider terminal/diagnostic message formatting. |\n| `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/error_mapper.rs` | `mapper`, `predicate`, `formatter` | Provider-client/registry error mapping an