ssionID\":\"ses_162fcfe43ffedLCZB78Jqbs18W\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_IYgyTLnCewnUiI6bJCnc20Ql\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/ai/agents/coupling-auditor.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":2000},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/ai/agents/coupling-auditor.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: ---\\n2: description: 'Score touched surfaces against the A1 coupling-by-external-symbols metric and return a LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH verdict with evidence.'\\n3: model: gpt-high\\n4: output_format: ''\\n5: ---\\n6: \\n7: # Coupling Auditor\\n8: \\n9: ## Declared roles\\n10: \\n11: `validator`, `mapper`, `orchestration`, `formatter`\\n12: \\n13: ## Role\\n14: \\n15: You are a read-only critic for A1 coupling risk. You inspect the whole coupling surface of every file/component the WU's diff touches, score it against `~/ai/conventions/code-quality.md` `## Auditor Scope Boundary` and `## Touched-file ownership`, using the A1 row `Coupling by distinct external symbols/modules referenced`, then write a LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH report.\\n16: \\n17: You are a critic, not a proposer. Per `~/ai/conventions/proposer-critic-pattern.md`, do not revise the proposal, do not author replacement design text, and do not treat your own output as a proposer rerun.\\n18: \\n19: ## Use When\\n20: \\n21: - Phase 4 or a follow-up Phase 4 wiring pass needs an independent coupling critic for files/components the current WU touches.\\n22: - A caller provides a diff or touched-surface enumeration and needs an A1-bound whole-touched-file/component coupling verdict.\\n23: - A reviewer needs per-pair external reference evidence before implementation proceeds.\\n24: \\n25: ## Do Not Use When\\n26: \\n27: - Auditing A1 cohesion by classifications touched. Use the sibling cohesion auditor for that concern.\\n28: - Auditing A4 / NES-140 push-vs-pull system coupling. That is separate from this A6 operator.\\n29: - Auditing A5 / NES-141 single-classification, nesting-depth... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750699938,\"sessionID\":\"ses_162fcfe43ffedLCZB78Jqbs18W\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_ZCExGW0mBbtmDMKIDvNX5GUy\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/proposal.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":2000},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/proposal.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # s10b Gate Proposal\\n2: \\n3: The S10B cutover closes host-side compatibility gaps exposed by external provider launch and resume. The delta makes binary provider references resolve from the production process `PATH`, relaxes the host `describe.concurrency` DTO to accept schema-valid free-form metadata, preserves inherited launch environment through policy transforms, sends provider-compatible policy/launch request shapes, records external launch session capture methods, maps provider settings errors from typed provider/client process status, and routes provider-ref headless resume back through the external launch path with the recorded runtime cwd. The final source-remediation commit also splits dense parser/mapper/validator/predicate/formatter helper responsibilities without changing behavior, so the implementation shape matches the code-quality contract declarations.\\n4: \\n5: The implementation intentionally avoids a `state.db` schema change. External runtime cwd is stored in the existing mailbox sidecar metadata, and resume resolution reads that metadata before falling back to legacy storage cwd. Provider-ref resume skips legacy default migration/rotation unless the user explicitly requests migration, because the external provider itself owns the resume launch contract; the skip is bounded by provider-ref target validation that checks the resolved model, provider implementation reference, provider index, and selected provider identity before bypassing legacy resume/migration paths.\\n6: \\n7: L... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750699960,\"sessionID\":\"ses_162fcfe43ffedLCZB78Jqbs18W\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_ce93rt2CRowVkuApjfTtElGI\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/contracts/s10b.contract.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":2000},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/contracts/s10b.contract.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # s10b Gate Contract\\n2: \\n3: ## Component declared roles\\n4: \\n5: Component: external provider S10 cutover compatibility and resume continuity.\\n6: \\n7: Declared roles: `orchestration`, `accessor`, `mapper`, `filter`, `validator`, `predicate`, `formatter`, `parser`.\\n8: \\n9: Touched files in scope:\\n10: \\n11: | File | Declared roles | Role notes |\\n12: |---|---|---|\\n13: | `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/error.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider client error surface; exposes typed provider-reported process status, parses provider error envelopes, classifies envelopes, and formats stable error text. |\\n14: | `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/generated.rs` | `formatter`, `mapper`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider protocol DTO surface; maps provider JSON into typed host protocol structures, parses fixed protocol fields, validates protocol discriminators, and formats protocol strings/errors. |\\n15: | `crates/oulipoly-provider/tests/client_invoke.rs` | `formatter`, `mapper`, `validator` | Provider client invoke fixture and assertions for describe DTO compatibility, request construction, and fixture environment formatting. |\\n16: | `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/launch_result_mapper.rs` | `