\":502,\"output\":209,\"reasoning\":0,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":39424}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1780750713588,\"sessionID\":\"ses_162fcfe43ffedLCZB78Jqbs18W\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e9d0382f2001KFy21k2rKudRnh\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e9d037e7c0010oAvoLG710iM9M\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_162fcfe43ffedLCZB78Jqbs18W\",\"snapshot\":\"7d43e6079037ffa5b36be151e36a4a9a74894e0a\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1780750720836,\"sessionID\":\"ses_162fcfe43ffedLCZB78Jqbs18W\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e9d0392e2001Eid8jui5mvlcs6\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e9d037e7c0010oAvoLG710iM9M\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_162fcfe43ffedLCZB78Jqbs18W\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The required code-quality convention confirms the A1 coupling row and the adapter/intrinsic rules: explicit declarations are required, adapter/intrinsic thresholds are LOW at <= 5 contracts/domains when all references are subordinate.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1780750717667,\"end\":1780750720833},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0ccf1fa93a57f80f016a24197da38081948d442990c6dd551b\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750720905,\"sessionID\":\"ses_162fcfe43ffedLCZB78Jqbs18W\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_1VJBO7bnvA63RTBeoga6T89p\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md\",\"offset\":600,\"limit\":600},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n600: - editing files is not Tier-3\\n601: - running tests is not Tier-3\\n602: - opening **draft** PRs is not Tier-3\\n603: - public promotion and other outward-facing actions follow the tiered-approval workflow\\n604: \\n605: ## Pause For Refactor\\n606: \\n607: This section owns the pause state model for existing-code refactor work discovered during an implementation WU. For the strategy boundary, cite `conventions/feature-development-workflow.md` `## Refactoring out of scope`; do not restate that rule elsewhere in this workflow.\\n608: \\n609: - trigger: an auditor, reviewer, or implementation step identifies existing-code structural refactor work that is outside touched-file/component ownership, or inside touched ownership but too large for the current WU, and material to continuing safely.\\n610: - pause evidence: record the current ticket id, branch, head SHA, worktree path, dirty status, failing or residual report paths, and the reason the refactor is outside touched ownership or requires decomposition.\\n611: - ticket/backend action: use the selected ticket backend to comment the pause evidence on the current ticket and apply the available pause/blocking status or label; if no status exists, use a clear blocking comment plus link relation.\\n612: - refactor-ticket filing: file a linked refactor-ticket with the bounded structural target, preserved-behavior requirement, evidence paths, and relationship to the paused WU.\\n613: - ACR-179 routing: run the refactor-ticket through the ACR-179 refactoring route, using `workflows/refactoring.md` and `agents/refactoring-orchestrator.md`.\\... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750720927,\"sessionID\":\"ses_162fcfe43ffedLCZB78Jqbs18W\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_SnJzKaHdDcC6tyGRL84kwBgs\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"Phase 6|per-component|code-quality|contract_path|Component declared roles\",\"path\":\"/home/nes/ai/workflows\",\"include\":\"implementation-pipeline.md\"},\"output\":\"Found 40 matches\\n/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md:\\n  Line 15:     - \\\"keeps tests and product code separated between Phase 6b and Phase 6c invocations\\\"\\n\\n  Line 34: This workflow sequences the implementation pipeline (orchestration), validates phase/gate/audit conditions (validator), and parses ticket/frontmatter/fenced-YAML and required-token shapes throughout Phase 0, Phase 2.5, Phase 3, Phase 4, Phase 6, and Phase 8 (parser). The R6 declared-roles expansion adds `parser` per the cohesion-auditor R5 evidence at lines 68, 320, 322, and 334.\\n\\n  Line 70: - keeps tests and product code separated between Phase 6b and Phase 6c invocations\\n\\n  Line 133: - `Phase 2.5 -> Phase 3 -> Phase 4 -> Phase 5 -> Phase 6 -> Phase 7 -> Phase 8 -> Phase 9 -> Phase 10`\\n\\n  Line 134: - Recursion edge: completed parent `Phase 6` component work may open a child recursion level that enters `level-open` and reuses the same Phase 6 contract/test/code path; the parent reaches `child-levels-open` only after candidate children have been considered for framing.\\n\\n  Line 142: `normal` is the default when `pipeline_entry_mode` is absent or explicitly `normal`. The orchestrator runs the existing Phase 0 ticket/worktree/bootstrap route and then continues through Phase 2.5, Phase 3, Phase 4, Phase 5, Phase 6, Phase 7, Phase 8, Phase 9, and Final/closure as before. It does not dispatch `~/ai/workflows/audit.md`, consume an audit bundle, import review findings, or switch modes based on stray fields.\\n\\n  Line 188: - Tests authored in **Phase 6b** and product code authored in **Phase 6c** **are** committed in t... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750720927,\"sessionID\":\"ses_162fcfe43ffedLCZB78Jqbs18W\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"grep\",\"callID\":\"call_0XSKgtnJwVzJSQFFn1yUIdvb\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"^diff --git\",\"path\":\"/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/gates\",\"include\":\"diff.patch\"},\"output\":\"Found 20 matches\\n/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/gates/diff.patch:\\n  Line 1: diff --git a/crates/oulipoly-provider/src/error.rs b/crates/oulipoly-provider/src/error.rs\\n\\n  Line 225: diff --git a/crates/oulipoly-provider/src/