.. (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1780750092972,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069809ffeuCPl3U2riKHvxp\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e9cfa0aa80012d64jg5TpLCs2w\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"403c4243a580298d324dfecb2f6f375f70a9445e\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e9cf9cbf4001xb4fK0kD3MawWN\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069809ffeuCPl3U2riKHvxp\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":78887,\"input\":39755,\"output\":216,\"reasoning\":516,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":38400}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1780750094163,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069809ffeuCPl3U2riKHvxp\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e9cfa0f50001KnbKP8rzhCs3ia\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e9cfa0acb001qQexo92109LWl3\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069809ffeuCPl3U2riKHvxp\",\"snapshot\":\"403c4243a580298d324dfecb2f6f375f70a9445e\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1780750098336,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069809ffeuCPl3U2riKHvxp\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e9cfa1f77001p86rGA6mMd4Cy4\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e9cfa0acb001qQexo92109LWl3\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069809ffeuCPl3U2riKHvxp\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I’m treating `diff.patch` and `touched-files.txt` as authoritative for audited source scope, as requested, and not widening to the gate artifacts themselves.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1780750098295,\"end\":1780750098333},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_04e80d1eac79944f016a24171244248193a7bb6e61add8b94a\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750098517,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069809ffeuCPl3U2riKHvxp\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_lI9LzIvlNcXQpdksGpcqd0oj\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md\",\"offset\":403,\"limit\":130},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n403: ## Phase 6 - Implementation (required; test/code separation)\\n404: \\n405: Implementation has three sub-steps.\\n406: The test writer and the code writer must be different agent invocations.\\n407: That rule is load-bearing: if the same agent writes both, the tests mirror the implementation instead of validating the contract.\\n408: Step 6a defines the level outer contract; during Step 6c, once passing evidence exists, post-prototype internal component contract derivation may be triggered.\\n409: When Step 6c's post-prototype derivation accepts internal components, current-layer integration tests for interactions between those component pairs are required as part of the same derivation evidence.\\n410: Rule: Step 6c may discover procedural obligations during implementation, but discovery does not relax the different-invocation rule; procedural tests still go through a separate Step 6b-style test-writer invocation.\\n411: After Step 6c has passing level evidence, the derivation trigger logic decides whether the level derives accepted internal component contracts, records an evidence-bearing halt/no-split when a trigger fires but no split earns granularity, or proceeds to Phase 7 unchanged when neither trigger arm fires.\\n412: \\n413: - Rule: Phase 6 firstness evidence is the Phase 6 process-tree review plus companion artifacts. The companion artifacts are the expected-process manifest, Step 6b prompt/log, Step 6c prompt/log, Step 6b output index, Step 6b output paths, and evidence that Step 6c consumed those outputs. For ACR-247 side-channel runs, that consumption evidence is th... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1780750098553,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069809ffeuCPl3U2riKHvxp\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e9cfa2075001D68j1B70SVmpc3\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"403c4243a580298d324dfecb2f6f375f70a9445e\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e9cfa0acb001qQexo92109LWl3\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069809ffeuCPl3U2riKHvxp\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":94163,\"input\":16214,\"output\":80,\"rea