1: # Code Quality Convention\\n2: \\n3: This convention defines code-shape rules for generated and reviewed code across the `~/ai/` ecosystem.\\n4: \\n5: ## Purpose\\n6: \\n7: This is the canonical, language-neutral code-shape rule list for generated and reviewed code; downstream auditors enforce these rules in their own passes, and this convention does not itself run checks.\\n8: \\n9: ## Scope\\n10: \\n11: These rules apply uniformly across Rust, TypeScript, Python, and any other project language. They apply to both human-authored and agent-authored code. They are review rules for ordinary PR review and for specialized auditor passes that inspect function shape, responsibility boundaries, duplicate handling, and cross-system coupling.\\n12: \\n13: `~/ai` markdown/operator/workflow/convention/routing/anchor structural guard requests are not code-quality checker authoring and are not pytest work. Structural-verification requests for those surfaces route to WRITE eval-spec authoring under `~/ai/conventions/evals.md`, with no narrower prohibition than that convention's binding enumeration: no `tools/<wu>-verify/<anything>.py`, no `tests/test_*.py`, no pytest imports or fixtures, and no pytest-shaped assertion code.\\n14: \\n15: The convention is intentionally language-neutral. A project may have local style rules for naming, formatting, framework boundaries, or idioms, but those local rules do not replace the code-shape requirements here.\\n16: \\n17: ## Declared roles\\n18: \\n19: `validator`, `mapper`\\n20: \\n21: ## Auditor Scope Boundary\\n22: \\n23: For every A1 auditor, the WU's diff identifies the touched file... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750081916,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_ZZmqeMGkUlDYxxsh1fO1z1cs\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/ai/conventions/proposer-critic-pattern.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":2000},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/ai/conventions/proposer-critic-pattern.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # Proposer / Critic Pattern\\n2: \\n3: ## What this convention is\\n4: \\n5: This convention names the proposer/critic meta-pattern for workflow authors, orchestrator authors, and operator authors. It is a shared rule document, not an orchestrator, and it does not subsume the existing instantiations. Per `~/ai/VALUES.md` § Composition over flag-stuffing, workflows compose their own proposers, critics, dispatch rules, and acceptance vocabulary.\\n6: \\n7: ## Two sides\\n8: \\n9: A proposer authors or revises a reviewable artifact: a proposal, plan, roadmap, diff, or another work product named by the workflow. A critic evaluates that artifact and returns a verdict or findings under the workflow's dialect. The proposer and critic are different agents in different invocations.\\n10: \\n11: ## The cycle\\n12: \\n13: The pattern is a revise/review loop:\\n14: \\n15: 1. The proposer authors the artifact from the workflow inputs.\\n16: 2. Critics run against the artifact and the relevant problem/context.\\n17: 3. Critics return a verdict.\\n18: 4. Any non-accept verdict triggers a fresh proposer dispatch with the failing critic outputs as input.\\n19: 5. After revision, every critic that belongs to the pass re-runs against the revised artifact.\\n20: \\n21: Old accepts are discarded after a substantive proposal revision because they reviewed a superseded artifact. They cannot be carried forward as acceptance for the same pass.\\n22: \\n23: ## Acceptance\\n24: \\n25: Acceptance requires all required critics return LOW, or the workflow's accept equivalent, for the same current artifact. A workflow may ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750081916,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_6a2WPTG74hKuKDld2x49Sc6u\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/ai/conventions/risk-profile.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":2000},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/ai/conventions/risk-profile.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # Risk Profile — Conventions\\n2: \\n3: A risk profile is the artifact that decides how rigorously the implementation pipeline runs. It is produced in **Phase 2.5** of `~/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md` and consumed by Phases 3, 4, and 5. It is not just a number — it is a **per-surface scored map** of where on the touched terrain the work is risky and where it is not, plus a single rolled-up verdict.\\n4: \\n5: The principle is simple: when there is real risk, be exhaustive. When there is not, lean on tests and move fast. Per-surface scoring is what lets a single ticket be lean in some places and exhaustive in others without choosing the wrong global mode.\\n6: \\n7: A project that adopts this convention also maintains a **project-level risk profile** (`<project>/planning/risk-profile.md`) that aggregates per-WU profiles into the project's high-risk surfaces, which then drive `~/ai/workflows/risk-reduction.md` work between tickets.\\n8: \\n9: **Prototypes score risk at the end, not during.** Per `~/ai/workflows/build-prototype.md`, a prototype run produces its risk profile in Phase P3 (Present), against the surfaces the prototype actually touched (which may be different from what was anticipated). Prototypes do **not** run per-surface mode during the hack phase; lean/exhaustive mode is irrelevant when there are no mid-flight gates to apply it to. The prototype's `dossier/risk-profile.md` follows the same scoring rules as a Phase-2.5 risk profile and aggregates into the project profile the same way; the only difference is the timing.\\n10: \\n11: ## Scoring axes\\n12: \\n13: Each touched surfac... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750081917,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_4Bdob4CXeeenzYe6BypkKQny\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":3000},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: ---\\n2: workflow:\\n3:   id: implementation-pipeline\\n4: workflow_dispatch_contract:\\n5:   orchestrator: \\\"implementation-pipeline-orchestrator\\\"\\n6:   inputs:\\n7:     - \\\"ticket id and branch, worktree, scratch, and planning paths\\\"\\n8:     - \\\"non-empty ticket description from the configured Jira or Linear ticket system\\\"\\n9:     - \\\"optional pipeline_entry_mode normal, review_first, or plug_existing_review with audit target or existing review bundle inputs when that mode requires them\\\"\\n10:   expectations:\\n11:     - \\\"runs research, proposal, shared apply-gate-set risk/review boundaries, hookpoint, implementation, readiness, PR, and audit phases\\\"\\n12:     - \\\"defaults to normal mode; review_first runs audit after Phase 0 and before Phase 2.5, while plug_existing_review validates a current audit bundle before Phase 3 consumes it\\\"\\n13:     - \\\"defer-to-prototype carry-forward includes prototype-test PR URL, branch, test paths/node IDs, marker reason, and acceptance criterion: Remove the prototype-pending: markers and make these tests pass.\\\"\\n14:     - \\\"uses apply-gate-set caller modes implementation-phase-4, implementation-phase-6, and implementation-phase-8 for Phase 4/6/8 gate sets; human gates are limited to Phase 2.5 review and NEEDS_INPUT new-value questions\\\"\\n15:     - \\\"keeps tests and product code separated between Phase 6b and Phase 6c invocations\\\"\\n16:   outputs:\\n17:     - \\\"planning artifacts under the per-WU planning directory\\\"\\n18:     - \\\"tested repository diff and draft PR URL when the work proceeds\\\"\\n19:     - \\\"ticket comments and audit-history ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750081941,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_Mo1JTFAbReAHhuvtBZ7qLPch\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/gates/diff.patch\",\"offset\":1415,\"limit\":4000},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/gates/diff.patch</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1415: +            .execute(request)\\n1416: +            .map(|output| output.result)\\n1417: +            .map_err(|err| err.to_string());\\n1418: +    }\\n1419:      executor::cli::execute_resume_optional_prompt_with_model_identity(\\n1420:          provider,\\n1421:          provider_index,\\n1422: @@ -361,12 +387,36 @@ fn execute_resume_attempt_command(\\n1423:          Some(invocation_env),\\n1424:          executor::cli::ResumePayload {\\n1425:              session_id: &input.resolved.active_session_id,\\n1426: -            strategy,\\n1427: +            strategy: strategy.expect(\\\"legacy resume target must have a resume strategy\\\"),\\n1428:          },\\n1429:          input.resolved.model_name.as_deref().unwrap_or(\\\"<unknown>\\\"),\\n1430:      )\\n1431:  }\\n1432:  \\n1433: +fn provider_ref_resume_executor_request(\\n1434: +    input: &ResumeAttemptInput<'_>,\\n1435: +    provider: &oulipoly_config::ProviderConfig,\\n1436: +    provider_index: usize,\\n1437: +    prompt_mode: oulipoly_config::PromptMode,\\n1438: +    invocation_env: &str,\\n1439: +) -> Option<ExecutorServiceRequest> {\\n1440: +    let model = input.resolved.model.as_ref()?;\\n1441: +    model.provider.as_ref()?;\\n1442: +    Some(\\n1443: +        ExecutorServiceRequest::EffectiveWithStartKnownProviderSessionId {\\n1444: +            model: model.clone(),\\n1445: +            provider: provider.clone(),\\n1446: +            provider_index,\\n1447: +            prompt_mode,\\n1448: +            prompt: input.answer.unwrap_or_default().to_string(... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"step_finish\",\"timestamp\":1780750081972,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e9cf9dfaf001buI2PAgopnJYyo\",\"reason\":\"tool-calls\",\"snapshot\":\"403c4243a580298d324dfecb2f6f375f70a9445e\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e9cf9b3010014Zo6j4NtV95njH\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"type\":\"step-finish\",\"tokens\":{\"total\":52339,\"input\":29446,\"output\":212,\"reasoning\":153,\"cache\":{\"write\":0,\"read\":22528}},\"cost\":0}}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1780750082985,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e9cf9e3a7001W0xog91eVVZHiG\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e9cf9dfd0001bvRJfAX4pcjTGk\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"snapshot\":\"403c4243a580298d324dfecb2f6f375f70a9445e\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1780750093056,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e9cf9f737001NYUU7pp6aTFFO0\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e9cf9dfd0001bvRJfAX4pcjTGk\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"The Phase 6 contract is readable and declares the component role union `orchestration`, `accessor`, `mapper`, `filter`, `validator`, `predicate`, `formatter`, `parser`; I’m checking the Phase 6 workflow rules and the current touched source files against that set before writing the report.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1780750087991,\"end\":1780750093051},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_0e2676025ddb8b78016a241707f2248190811c712acb1b645d\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750093167,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_RvNudXlmQkQT7X5h6x5TWhTA\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md\",\"offset\":520,\"limit\":2200},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/ai/workflows/implementation-pipeline.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n520: - Loop primitive: `~/ai/tools/coderabbit_review_driver.py review-loop ${repo} ${pr_num} --worktree-path ${worktree_path} --mode ${coderabbit_trigger_mode}`.\\n521: - The driver owns the full loop: trigger or auto-skip an already-pending trigger, wait for ack, enforce the 300-second minimum cadence between loop-owned polls, dispatch one fixer invocation per actionable in-diff comment, preserve each structured outcome, push fixed commits, post reply files, trigger incremental follow-up reviews, and continue until terminal.\\n522: - `terminal_reason=approved` is CodeRabbit success.\\n523: - `terminal_reason=no_value_provided` is accepted convergence when every actionable in-diff comment in the latest iteration was assessed `review_provided_value: false`.\\n524: - `needs_caller_decision=true` surfaces valuable `rejected` or `deferred` per-comment outcomes to the root caller without re-triggering.\\n525: - The orchestrator must not compose its own trigger/poll/dispatch/retrigger loop, must not use inline `gh pr view ... statusCheckRollup` polling, must not inline CodeRabbit comment bodies, and must not synthesize an empty review pass.\\n526: - If the pipeline creates or reuses a PR, it writes `${scratch_dir}/pr-url.txt`; Phase 9 reuses that URL instead of creating a duplicate PR.\\n527: \\n528: ## Phase 8 - Post-Review Gates\\n529: \\n530: - These are the PR-opening gates on the actual diff.\\n531: - Policy: dispatch `apply-gate-set(caller_mode=implementation-phase-8)` after Phase 7 readiness and optional review delegation, before draft PR movement.\\n532: - The Phase 8 gate-set invent... (line truncated to 2000 chars)","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/.scratch/code-quality/s10b/logs/cohesion-auditor.log","text":"OULIPOLY_INVOCATION={\"source\":\"opencode5\",\"id\":\"578ea1bf-aa40-445a-b245-3d5f31d089b7\"}\nOULIPOLY_SESSION={\"agent_runner_chain_id\":\"4396a989-412c-4a60-b58d-fbca8b5fa8c2\",\"agent_runner_invocation_id\":\"578ea1bf-aa40-445a-b245-3d5f31d089b7\",\"id\":\"578ea1bf-aa40-445a-b245-3d5f31d089b7\",\"provider_name\":\"opencode5\",\"provider_session_id\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"resume_input_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\"}\n{\"type\":\"step_start\",\"timestamp\":1780750055313,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e9cf9778e0010s9VBI9WcjeyVD\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e9cf968c7001GLpllYlYGPoo98\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"snapshot\":\"403c4243a580298d324dfecb2f6f375f70a9445e\",\"type\":\"step-start\"}}\n{\"type\":\"text\",\"timestamp\":1780750070342,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"id\":\"prt_e9cf9a018001KbFwwtUoYsfg7r\",\"messageID\":\"msg_e9cf968c7001GLpllYlYGPoo98\",\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Reading the auditor operator, contract, proposal, touched-file list, and source diff to constrain the audit to the requested component.\",\"time\":{\"start\":1780750065688,\"end\":1780750070334},\"metadata\":{\"openai\":{\"itemId\":\"msg_038f41dbb95fb0e0016a2416f1aa1881978cabc0da2b36cca6\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}}}}\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750070435,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_CCOZQGCUsJ1f7CGynbj1Q1hv\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/ai/agents/cohesion-auditor.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":2000},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/ai/agents/cohesion-auditor.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: ---\\n2: description: 'Score touched surfaces against the A1 cohesion-by-classifications-touched metric and return a LOW/HIGH verdict with evidence.'\\n3: model: gpt-high\\n4: output_format: ''\\n5: ---\\n6: \\n7: # Cohesion Auditor\\n8: \\n9: ## Role\\n10: \\n11: You are a read-only critic for A1 cohesion risk. You inspect every file/component the WU's diff touches, score the whole touched file/component against `~/ai/conventions/code-quality.md` `## Auditor Scope Boundary` and `## Touched-file ownership`, using the A1 row `Cohesion by classifications touched`, then write a LOW/HIGH report.\\n12: \\n13: You are a critic, not a proposer. Per `~/ai/conventions/proposer-critic-pattern.md`, do not revise the proposal, do not author replacement design text, and do not treat your own output as a proposer rerun.\\n14: \\n15: ## Use When\\n16: \\n17: - Phase 4 or a follow-up Phase 4 wiring pass needs an independent cohesion critic for the files/components the current WU touches.\\n18: - A caller provides a diff or touched-surface enumeration and needs an A1-bound whole-touched-file/component cohesion verdict.\\n19: - A reviewer needs per-component classification evidence before implementation proceeds.\\n20: \\n21: ## Do Not Use When\\n22: \\n23: - Auditing A1 coupling by external symbols or modules. Use the sibling coupling auditor for that concern.\\n24: - Auditing A4 / NES-140 push-vs-pull system coupling. That is separate from this A6 operator.\\n25: - Auditing A5 / NES-141 nesting-depth, inline-function, or duplicate-responsibility failures.\\n26: - Tracing cross-language dependency graphs without scoring A1 cohesion. ... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750070435,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_t3uJLKr2Hvuwm4XFu7g9rX2q\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/proposal.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":2000},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/proposal.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # s10b Gate Proposal\\n2: \\n3: The S10B cutover closes host-side compatibility gaps exposed by external provider launch and resume. The delta makes binary provider references resolve from the production process `PATH`, relaxes the host `describe.concurrency` DTO to accept schema-valid free-form metadata, preserves inherited launch environment through policy transforms, sends provider-compatible policy/launch request shapes, records external launch session capture methods, maps provider settings errors from typed provider/client process status, and routes provider-ref headless resume back through the external launch path with the recorded runtime cwd. The final source-remediation commit also splits dense parser/mapper/validator/predicate/formatter helper responsibilities without changing behavior, so the implementation shape matches the code-quality contract declarations.\\n4: \\n5: The implementation intentionally avoids a `state.db` schema change. External runtime cwd is stored in the existing mailbox sidecar metadata, and resume resolution reads that metadata before falling back to legacy storage cwd. Provider-ref resume skips legacy default migration/rotation unless the user explicitly requests migration, because the external provider itself owns the resume launch contract; the skip is bounded by provider-ref target validation that checks the resolved model, provider implementation reference, provider index, and selected provider identity before bypassing legacy resume/migration paths.\\n6: \\n7: L... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750070436,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_nxmTXFltIp7pnz5KAqhLexog\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/contracts/s10b.contract.md\",\"offset\":1,\"limit\":2000},\"output\":\"<path>/home/nes/projects/agent-runner/worktrees/age-pid-sidecar/planning/s10b-gate/contracts/s10b.contract.md</path>\\n<type>file</type>\\n<content>\\n1: # s10b Gate Contract\\n2: \\n3: ## Component declared roles\\n4: \\n5: Component: external provider S10 cutover compatibility and resume continuity.\\n6: \\n7: Declared roles: `orchestration`, `accessor`, `mapper`, `filter`, `validator`, `predicate`, `formatter`, `parser`.\\n8: \\n9: Touched files in scope:\\n10: \\n11: | File | Declared roles | Role notes |\\n12: |---|---|---|\\n13: | `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/error.rs` | `accessor`, `formatter`, `mapper`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider client error surface; exposes typed provider-reported process status, parses provider error envelopes, classifies envelopes, and formats stable error text. |\\n14: | `crates/oulipoly-provider/src/generated.rs` | `formatter`, `mapper`, `parser`, `predicate`, `validator` | Provider protocol DTO surface; maps provider JSON into typed host protocol structures, parses fixed protocol fields, validates protocol discriminators, and formats protocol strings/errors. |\\n15: | `crates/oulipoly-provider/tests/client_invoke.rs` | `formatter`, `mapper`, `validator` | Provider client invoke fixture and assertions for describe DTO compatibility, request construction, and fixture environment formatting. |\\n16: | `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src/executor/external_provider/launch_result_mapper.rs` | `accessor`, `filter`, `mapper`, `predicate` | External LaunchExit event/session extraction, non-empty session-id filtering, and runtime result/session capture mapping. |\\n17: | `crates/oulipoly-runtime/src... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"timestamp\":1780750070436,\"sessionID\":\"ses_163069850ffeylL7yC07vq9KHo\",\"part\":{\"type\":\"tool\",\"tool\":\"read\",\"callID\":\"call_GT3yvvKolvoJr1fPv1S70jUb\",\"state\":{\"status\":\"completed\",\"input\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/nes/projects/agent-runne